WEBVTT

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.970
<i>I hated this island.</i>

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.500
<i>It was too cramped.</i>

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:24.240
<i>The land was cramped, 
the relationships were cramped...</i>

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.600
<i>The adults knew nothing 
of the outside world,</i>

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.050
<i>and they refused to learn.</i>

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.300
<i>They just lived peaceful 
lives and then died.</i>

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.150
<i>Everything around me felt so small.</i>

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.800
<i>I felt like I was suffocating.</i>

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.850
<i>I couldn't stand it.</i>

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.010
<i>A far more amazing world 
lay beyond the sea.</i>

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.560
<i>A place where I could burn off my 
energy and pursue my own potential.</i>

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.080
<i>So I...</i>

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.760
<i>became a mercenary.</i>

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.200
<i>That was fifteen years ago.</i>

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.070
<i>As I hopped from one nation to 
the next, I realized something.</i>

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.840
<i>In some places, there were people 
fighting for peace in their homelands.</i>

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.260
<i>In other places, people fought 
to keep their families,</i>

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.100
<i>their friends, and their loved ones safe.</i>

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.390
<i>That tiny, cramped island,</i>

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.740
<i>Jiffon Island, the land that saw no wars,</i>

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.660
<i>was the home they wanted.</i>

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.170
Talk about ironic.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.300
Stop!

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.340
<i>Who knew I'd learn that 
after abandoning it?</i>

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.420
<i>To me, this island is...</i>

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.340
You look so dumb.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.410
The sounds that makes are way too cool.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.090
What're you doing out here?

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:57.420
Great Hero...

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.730
Weren't you on the boat?

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.590
Yes. My name's Raji.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.730
I was just inspecting the land, but...

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.950
I ended up stranded here.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.960
You should get off the 
mountain while you can.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:16.020
Poisonous volcanic gases will probably 
be drifting down here soon.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.100
Y-Yes, you're right. I'll do that.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.450
Um, where are you two headed?

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.260
Oh, just...

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.730
to do some hero work.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:38.840
<i>That dragon is definitely the one sucking 
the life force out of the islanders.</i>

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.030
<i>But why? And why right now?</i>

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.390
Hey, look!

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.550
<i>Is that...</i>

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.310
There you are, dragon!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.150
Die!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.700
<b>Dead</b>

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.700
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.700
<b>Torii Keita</b>

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:09.070
<i>Nope! Nope! Nope! Nope! No way in hell!</i>

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.380
<i>There's no way I can beat that thing now!</i>

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:13.780
<i>If I can't beat it, so I won't beat it!</i>

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.850
<i>Is there a way to drive it 
back without beating it?</i>

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.880
<i>What does it want, anyway?</i>

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.750
<i>Sucking out life force... 
to replenish its energy?</i>

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.850
<i>Is this basically how it eats?</i>

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.390
<i>If it is...</i>

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:29.740
<i>That attack it just used would've 
been a waste of energy.</i>

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.290
<i>There'd be no point in replenishing it.</i>

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.970
<i>Is that why it's staying on the 
mountaintop and not chasing us?</i>

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.090
<i>Which would mean...</i>

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:41.850
<i>Maybe it's an extremely 
energy-inefficient creature?</i>

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.820
<i>If I zombie myself to get it to 
keep breathing a bunch of fire,</i>

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.560
<i>will it use up its MP and grow weak?</i>

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:49.610
<i>No...</i>

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:51.590
<i>That won't work.</i>

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.940
<i>It would suck out all the islanders' 
life force before that.</i>

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.890
<i>What can I do?</i>

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.590
<i>For every type of magic user,</i>

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:05.340
<i>the closer you are to the target you're 
taking MP from, the better it works.</i>

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.750
<i>If the same rule applies to the dragon...</i>

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.420
They all look even worse than before.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:13.690
Why is this happening?

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.000
Someone's castin' magic on 'em.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.160
Magic?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.680
Drain magic.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:21.990
It's high-level magic that only 
powerful sorcerers can use.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:25.060
Yana, Väikedaam can use magic, right?

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.750
Isn't there anything you can do?

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.200
Ow...

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:33.400
Our magic ain't nearly strong enough to face 
such a high-level magic user head-on.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.840
If I at least knew the spell,

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.120
I could stop it from suckin' 
out people's strength...

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:42.320
<i>First, I have to get all the 
islanders away from the island!</i>

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.000
<i>That's the best way to drive 
it back without fighting!</i>

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.140
<i>He's still there?!</i>

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.350
<i>I had to get a little violent...</i>

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:59.140
<i>But I can't afford to waste any time!</i>

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.220
Well done, Hero. You figured it out.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.350
You're right.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:11.450
I am the Dragon Bishop who 
summoned the Darassuede Dragon.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.810
There's a canyon up ahead, and you're...

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.960
dropping... me... into... it?!

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:21.980
Huh?

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.310
Huh?

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:25.450
Huh?

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:28.650
Huh?

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.000
Huh?

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.090
Huh?!

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:39.690
You didn't actually know?!

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.600
Well, I do now!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.620
I'm not totally sure 
what's going on, but...

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.250
Dragon Bishop?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.550
Summoned?

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.300
Does that mean...

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:55.760
You're the one who brought 
the orcs to this island?!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.500
Apprevio... Exflanma...

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:10.790
<i>Magic users in this world have to 
recite incantations to use spells!</i>

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.230
Ignisfit...

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.460
<i>So while he's doing that...</i>

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.550
Breath of Fire!

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.510
<b>Dead</b>

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.510
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.510
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.600
<i>That was one quick incantation!</i>

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.150
I'm back!

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.800
<i>I've already been killed three times.</i>

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.930
<i>On top of being an instant kill, 
his magic is way too hard to dodge!</i>

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.770
<i>Go, Torii!</i>

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.300
Take that!

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.240
The bastard dodged it!

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.090
<i>Damn it! Sneak attacks won't work, either?!</i>

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:43.370
Huh?

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.090
Yo, so... he's an enemy, right?

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:50.290
Abeavalanche, oledograkiesims...

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.630
Yes, he is, but why did you come here?!

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.310
We could have surrounded him!

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:51.350
Uh...

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.020
Cold Breath!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.140
<b>Dead</b>

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.140
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.140
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.140
<b>Dead</b>

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.140
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.140
<b>Torii Keita</b>

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.640
I had heard that heroes don't die.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.980
This is a waste of my time.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.780
<i>The ones we really can't allow to 
be attacked are the Väikedaam.</i>

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.240
Wait, is he gonna...

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:17.820
Who's there?!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.880
Tch, I missed.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:23.410
Huh? You're... Raji from block three?!

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.980
Aoiu, I have nothing against you,

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:28.870
but to keep the heroes 
quiet, I need you to die.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:32.260
Apprevio... Exflanma... Ignisfit...

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:33.920
Breath of Fire!

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.820
<i>I can't believe Raji turned 
out to be a magic user.</i>

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:45.850
<i>There's no way I'll stand a chance 
against his strength by myself.</i>

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.210
<i>Raji from block three...</i>

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.410
<i>The child prodigy who learned to stand, walk,</i>

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:53.880
<i>and talk faster than any of the other kids.</i>

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:56.510
<i>He earned everyone's respect 
as a design engineer...</i>

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:58.740
<i>That's right!</i>

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.900
<i>The one who started saying 
we should build houses</i>

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.210
<i>on the land that the lava 
swallowed up was...</i>

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.170
Yes, it's all right.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:09.260
The development of our island is what 
we should all be working toward.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.040
How long...

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.470
Tell me!

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:18.280
How long have you been planning all this?!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.330
Apprevio...

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:23.620
<i>The mastermind was on 
this island all along!</i>

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:28.140
<i>Yet we brought mercenaries out here 
an' waged war on the orcs...</i>

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.860
<i>and let so many die.</i>

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.070
<i>It's all our fault...</i>

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.040
Ignisfit...

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:42.540
Breath of Fire!

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:46.880
Ow, that's hot!

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.950
<i>Great Hero?</i>

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.750
I knew you'd show up.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:53.800
This way!

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:59.020
<i>Why? Why are you...</i>

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:03.020
<i>After all the awful stuff 
we put you through...</i>

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.670
Aoiu-san.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.120
I need to ask for a favor.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.080
Oh?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:27.240
You're finally giving up? Then, die now!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.000
Breath of...

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.300
Raji!

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:32.880
Don't move!

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.960
m 0 0 l 260 0 l 260 170 l 0 170

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.960
[Magic Catalysts]

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.960
Each component of a Wizard's gear is made with a
piece of amber containing a part of one of three
magical bugs, a salamander, a gnome, or a sylphid,
as a catalyst. The catalyst can boost the strength of
the magic of all Wizards who touch it. Because
Väikedaam undergo a slight degree of magic training,
they also possess a creature magic catalyst.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:46.270
<i>Creature magic can increase the 
persuasiveness of one's words.</i>

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:49.720
<i>My magic and Aoiu-san's might 
not be enough individually,</i>

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:53.360
<i>but if we use magic with the same catalyst, 
which works as an amplifier...</i>

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:04.020
Damn it! Don't block it!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.220
Torii!

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:08.710
After him!

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:09.820
R-Right!

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.160
When he did that...

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:24.270
I thought you were gonna kiss 
me for a second, Yuusuke...

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.960
What the hell is that? Nobody told 
me there'd be stuff like that!

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.630
I ain't never seen it before.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:38.310
Raji prob'ly dropped it when he ran off.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:41.700
Medicine? No... some kind of magic tool?

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:42.620
Huh?

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.540
I've seen this flashy color 
somewhere before...

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.820
Oh, yeah!

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.730
See?

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.590
"See" what?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.760
You saw it back then?

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.640
I've got a great memory, huh?

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:02.660
Took you too long to recall it, though.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:05.990
What is it?

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:08.210
The absorption of power has weakened.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:09.700
The flow has changed...

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:12.050
Could this be...

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:16.340
It is! No doubt about it!

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:17.890
Yana?

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:25.640
There it is!

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:30.760
The six-star magic circle! I knew it!

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.510
Six-star magic circle?

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.740
Yeah. We gotta erase it!

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.490
Okay!

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.100
I feel a lot better now.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.090
It ain't over yet, though.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:48.420
This magic absorbs life force through 
six magic circles on the island.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:51.750
Then, when the flow of that life 
force changed earlier...

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.780
Someone erased one of the 
other magic circles.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:56.480
I bet it was Aoiu.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.080
Then, let's erase the rest ourselves!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:00.700
Huh?

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:04.630
We can hardly erase 'em if we 
don't know where they are.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:07.870
We just gonna follow the flow of 
life force and hope we find 'em?

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.310
That won't be necessary.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.380
Is that Jiffon Island?

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:16.460
Yes. I made it after I 
arrived on the island.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.480
I'm good at making maps.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:21.380
You're more than good. 
That's the work of a pro.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:27.650
Life force is sent to the mountaintop 
through six magic circles...

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:31.380
Which means they're most likely 
to be near the mountain.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:32.770
If they're spaced out evenly,

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:35.340
and the one we just erased is here...

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.760
Excellent!

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.180
Now I know the radius of the concentric 
circles with the mountain at their center.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:47.190
Now if we divide this into six equal 
parts at sixty-degree angles...

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.380
The elevation differences 
make it a challenge,

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:53.940
but you can't fool these eyes of mine!

00:14:55.750 --> 00:15:00.030
Mapmaking is so much more 
fun than fighting!

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.810
Why is this guy workin' 
as a mercenary, anyway?

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.090
It's done!

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.980
These are the locations 
of the remaining four!

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.910
That takes care of the last one.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.350
That should remove the magic.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:33.950
If this stops it from suckin' 
out the life force...

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.770
What was that sound?

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:56.820
The dragon's headin' back...

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:58.590
...toward the mountain.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:15.060
It's over.

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:21.590
We won, Cantil-san.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.760
<i>"I hate this island."</i>

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:46.470
<i>Even as he said that,</i>

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:50.730
<i>the one who stopped the boat from burning 
and saved the island's future was...</i>

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.010
Thanza-san...

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:13.970
<i>Love and hate are two 
sides of the same coin.</i>

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:18.370
<i>I don't want to admit it, 
but I'm not totally indifferent.</i>

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:20.680
<i>I...</i>

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.820
<i>I hate humans.</i>

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.630
Thank you for all you did.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.670
"Offer the Jiffon Buffo at Väikdamania."

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:45.370
That clears the quest!

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:51.080
We're only able to throw this 
festival 'cause of you heroes.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:53.710
We thank ya on behalf of all the islanders.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.540
No need for that.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:58.930
We only did it to fulfill our own goals.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.250
Still...

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.180
We'll never forget!

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:06.480
Everything we've experienced, 
everything we still need to learn...

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:11.050
As Väikedaam, we'll hand it all 
down to the next generation!

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.400
Aoiu, it's time.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.070
Oh... Right.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:27.830
If only you were from this world,

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.660
I would've wanted to retire 
by marrying you...

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:34.100
Wh-Wha... uh... er...

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.140
Well, take care!

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:48.760
So lame! You're such a virgin! 
Look how shifty you're acting!

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.600
First Kahvel-san, now her...

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:00.080
Why is a guy like him so 
popular in this world?

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:04.220
Who knows? Maybe because 
he's not as reserved here?

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.290
I think it's because he treated 
them like real people.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.910
Unlike how he treats us.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:21.540
<i>I've been adrift for more than a day.</i>

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:23.990
<i>Maybe this is the end of the road for me...</i>

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:27.260
Oh!

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:29.110
Hey!

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:30.250
Huh?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.160
One of the mercenaries from the island?

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.310
They said he was a former general,

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.720
but look how far he's fallen.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.240
Wha—

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:44.110
Cool!

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.550
<i>What was that? What in 
the world just happened?</i>

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:57.080
<i>And was that powerful magic...</i>

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:01.860
You're...

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:05.340
The great sorceress Fatina?

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:09.290
What's this? Have we met?

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:14.940
<b>All They Can Do Is Look Up at It</b>

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.640
<i>Nothing beats being in my own hometown.</i>

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:07.210
Now, as your reward for clearing 
the quest, you may ask one ques.

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.220
Hey.

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:13.080
What was that Dragon Bishop trying to do?

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.120
That's your question?!

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:15.910
Revive the dragon!

00:22:19.050 --> 00:22:19.830
Bye!

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:21.240
Wait, that's it?

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:25.200
<i>Revive the dragon...</i>

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:31.020
<i>So was the scene I saw after clearing 
the third quest a possible future?</i>

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:40.730
<i>Frankly, at the time, I wouldn't have 
cared if Tokyo had been destroyed,</i>

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:42.070
<i>but if that future comes to pass...</i>

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:45.390
<i>this place won't be safe, either.</i>

00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:51.830
<i>He fought until the very end 
to protect his homeland.</i>

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:54.200
<i>And I...</i>

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:55.480
Hi.

00:22:55.990 --> 00:22:57.490
Whoa, you scared me!

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:01.450
One of the people you will meet in 
the near future will be the sixth.

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:02.280
Huh?

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:02.860
Bye.

00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:04.960
Hey, hang on!

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:08.780
Calling

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:10.210
Hey, Yuusuke!

00:23:10.210 --> 00:23:11.660
How've ya been?

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:13.910
Hey, long time no see.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:14.900
Wait, who's this?

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.190
Uh...

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:19.800
I came here 'cause the 
white girl told me so.

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:21.540
Huh?

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.910
Are you Yuusuke Yotsuya?

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:26.920
Next week on <i>Million Lives</i>...

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:33.640
<b></b>Shindou Heads to Hollywood?!

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:33.640
<b></b>The New Hero, Yotsuya's Grandma!

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:33.640
<b></b>The Kingdom of Goldia's
Three-Round Cooking Contest

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:33.640
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.620
"Shindou Heads to Hollywood!?"

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:30.720
"The New Hero, Yotsuya's Grandma!"

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:33.630
and "The Kingdom of Goldia's Three-Round 
Cooking Contest," three altogeth.

00:23:33.630 --> 00:23:35.930
Don't miss next week's episo!

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:37.920
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:37.930
<b>Rock, Paper, Scissors!</b>

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:39.800
Shining...
